    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-15T18:32:31+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T18:32:31+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T08:02:31Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T08:02:31Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system moving over the Tasman Sea extends a ridge over eastern SA until early next week, while a trough lies through the far northwest, before weakening over the weekend. A cold front is forecast to cross the Bight on Monday, extending a trough over western and southern SA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-15T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, most likely later this evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far west. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers north of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 32.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h turning northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 38.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
